			<div class="content" id="post-content-2789168">
									

<p>I couldn't manage what I wanted, but at least here I can sort of place.</p>
<p>Edit: i plan to post updates once the contest is over.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;DOUBLE&nbsp;EDIT&nbsp;</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Hide&nbsp;whatever</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>So to elaborate. I was struck with a great <em>angle</em> to approach the Hideous Mountain with the other day, and after schoolwork was finished I pushed myself to put this together as best I could. While I won't elaborate too deeply, it will ideally have a Series 1/Series 2 kind of feel and a running <em>theme</em> of something that I genuinely fear.</p>
<p>The barest undertones of that is in here, and I think I did pretty alright. But more will be added in the near future, after the contest. If it goes beyond adding to the transcript logs, I'll go to the Rewrite Team and get their input, and am willing to work from there.</p>
<p>This all comes after literal weeks of grappling with my first concept, a witch. But Fantem made a witch 3000 that at this time is doing fairly well, and for that I'm eternally thankful and in awe.</p>
<p>I'm just happy I could write something again.</p>
